process-send-array-free.m's sender on the machine's GPU, which holds one
of the arrays it sends at a time: a block of 2 MiB, and a few small blocks.
REQUIRES: amdgpu-gpu

RUN: merkc -O2 -fprocess-declarations --offload-arch=%offload-arch %libomp-flags %S/process-send-array-free.m -o %t2
RUN: %gpu-env MERK_CHECK_PROCESS_MEMORY=1 timeout -k 1 60 %t2 gpu 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --match-full-lines --strict-whitespace
CHECK:1048612.0
CHECK-NEXT:Mercury runtime: a GPU process held at most {{209[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]}} bytes of blocks at once
